cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use codegraph or its retrieval evaluation, please cite it as below."
title: "codegraph: a cited code-structure index for Python, Java and TypeScript/JavaScript, with a labelled retrieval evaluation"
abstract: >-
  codegraph indexes Python, Java, TypeScript and JavaScript repositories into a symbol graph and
  answers structural questions (definitions, callers, callees, inheritance, unused candidates,
  change impact, name search) with a symbol identity and a file:line citation for every result,
  over a CLI and a read-only MCP server. It
  ships a 74-question hand-labelled evaluation that compares the graph with a text-search
  baseline and records hashes of every input.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Karim
    given-names: Muhib
repository-code: "https://github.com/muhib-karim/codegraph"
url: "https://muhib-karim.github.io/codegraph/"
license: MIT
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-22"
keywords:
